message.content:
This is a trailer for towing, with a tipping cassette body. Heading 8716 covers trailers and semi-trailers. Self-loading or self-unloading trailers for agricultural purposes fall under 8716.20, but this one is industrial, so it is not covered there. Other trailers and semi-trailers for the transport of goods fall under 8716.39, and 8716.39.00 covers "Other" trailers. The 10-digit lines are 8716.39.0030 (dump trailers?), 8716.39.0090 (other), and so on.

The HTSUS 8716.39 structure is as follows. 8716.39.00 has the subheadings: 8716.39.0010 "Trailers: Fifth-wheel type... ", 8716.39.0030 "Other: Of iron or steel?", and 8716.39.0090 "Other". I recall that 8716.39.0030 is "Trailers and semi-trailers of the container chassis type", 8716.39.0040 is "Other: Dump trailers"?, and 8716.39.0090 is "Other". The 8716.39.00 listing as I remember it is: 8716.39.0010 "Trailers designed for use with tractors... (Van type?)", 8716.39.0020 "Tank trailers", 8716.39.0030 "Container chassis", 8716.39.0040 "Dump trailers"?, 8716.39.0050 "Livestock", 8716.39.0090 "Other". I am not certain of these, but a tipping cassette trailer is akin to a dump trailer, though the cassette is removable. I'll go with 8716.39.0090 as the safest choice.

